    "narrative": "Today\u2019s lineup is anchored by **Pete Crow-Armstrong**, our highest-rated starter at 82.13. Facing Ober, **Pete Crow-Armstrong** benefits from an elite combination of favorable SP skill, a 14% platoon boost, and a projected wind-out condition. Crucially, his speed profile against a slow-delivery pitcher makes him a prime target for stolen bases, our scarcest category. **Christian Yelich** (72.74) and **Kazuma Okamoto** (70.30) follow closely, both capitalizing on positive platoon splits against Alcantara and Kay respectively. **Lars Nootbaar** (67.77) also warrants attention; despite a standard base projection, he enters the day with a massive 19% boost derived from the matchup against a high-ERA arm in Kelly, making him an undervalued asset in today's 5x5 hunt.\n\nThe most difficult decision on the bench was **Chase Meidroth**, who finished just shy of our starting threshold with a 36.69 score. While **Chase Meidroth** has shown flashes of potential, the combination of a tough SP matchup (Miles, 3.33 xERA) and a sub-optimal spot in the bottom of the order suppressed his efficiency below our strict 40.0 floor, forcing us to bench him to preserve our limited game caps. We are also monitoring the status of **Yordan Alvarez** (59.18); although he remains a lock in the lineup, his matchup against a quality arm like Kremer tempered his score relative to his elite 0.475 xwOBA. We remain focused on the efficiency of **Dillon Dingler** (52.34) and **Junior Caminero** (60.63), both of whom are positioned to provide solid output, provided they handle their respective left-handed matchups effectively. With **Trea Turner**, **Kyle Schwarber**, and **Hyeseong Kim** unavailable today, the Zebras are relying heavily on the top-tier speed and plate discipline of our active starters to gain ground in the standings.",
